.TH geectl-remote-delete-file 1  "geectl-remote-delete-file 0.2.3" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-remote\-delete\-file \- Delete a file from a package. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the deletion. The general form of `delete\-link`: deleting `_link` here issues the same delete as `delete\-link`. Deleting a file that is already gone is refused by the server (NotFound). The server records the delete with the fixed comment `removed <file>`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl remote delete\-file\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPROJECT\fR> <\fIPACKAGE\fR> <\fIFILE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Delete a file from a package. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the deletion. The general form of `delete\-link`: deleting `_link` here issues the same delete as `delete\-link`. Deleting a file that is already gone is refused by the server (NotFound). The server records the delete with the fixed comment `removed <file>`
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project the package lives in
.TP
<\fIPACKAGE\fR>
The package the file lives in
.TP
<\fIFILE\fR>
The file to delete
.SH VERSION
v0.2.3
